Description: native Clojure dialect on LLVM with seamless C++ interop
 jank is a general-purpose programming language which embraces the
 interactive, functional, value-oriented nature of Clojure and the desire
 for the native runtime and performance of C++. It compiles to native code
 through LLVM, with a JIT for interactive development and ahead-of-time
 compilation of programs, and can call into C++ directly.
 .
 jank is alpha quality software. This package is a snapshot of upstream's
 main branch, built against Debian's clang-22. The installed compiler
 refers to clang-22 at runtime for its JIT, so the package depends on the
 same upstream clang-22 release it was built with and must be rebuilt when
 trixie moves to a new clang-22 point release.
 .
 Ahead-of-time compilation with the dynamic runtime (jank compile --runtime
 dynamic) links against libLLVM and libclang-cpp and needs the recommended
 llvm-22-dev and libclang-cpp22-dev; the default static runtime does not.
